o-prirode-likantropii-name = On the Nature of Lycanthropy
o-prirode-likantropii-desc = Authored by Merlin Temnova...
o-prirode-likantropii-content = [head=3]Deconstruction of a Myth[/head]


    {"If I were paid one silver coin every time another unwashed villein, trembling, tells tales of \"wolf-men bitten in the forest\", I would already have bought this wretched fort solely for the pleasure of razing it to the ground. Truly, it is astonishing how deep the ignorance of common folk runs when they attempt to explain complex magical aberrations through the bites of rabid dogs."}


    {"Let us establish the truth once and for all. Lycanthropy is, de facto, neither an infection nor a contagious malady. It is a divine curse of the purest sort, its modus operandi inseparably bound to Zaygo, goddess of deceit and treachery. The fact that the local churchmen have still failed to identify this obvious correlation causes me genuine intellectual grief."}


    {"A werewolf in its true nature is not a mindless predator. Zaygo does not gift her carriers with primitive rabies. Her curse transforms the subject into a lethal and, most importantly, thinking entity. Physiological metamorphosis is merely the instrument. The subject receives colossal physical power for the methodical, cunning extermination of those around it. A werewolf can brilliantly mimic an honest citizen, weave intrigues, and strike at the exact moment you turn your back. Therein lies the perverse aesthetic of Zaygo's treachery."}


    {"My primary observations prove that containing this threat requires neither pitchforks nor garlic, but delicate magical diagnostics. One must identify those hypocrites who secretly serve the Goddess of Deceit, skillfully hiding their bestial essence beneath the masks of respectable soldiers and port laborers."}


    {"Nevertheless, while the local garrison tries to solve the problem with shouting and rusty steel, I intend to complete the autopsy of the specimen acquired. May Great Magnus have mercy upon my sense of smell, for this biological substance stinks quite unbearably."}

issledovatelskaya-rukopis-name = research manuscript
issledovatelskaya-rukopis-desc = A heavy book that miraculously survived the fire. The margins of the open page are covered with complex geometric diagrams and narrow columns of calculations. The lower part of the sheet has burned away completely, making the formulas and further derivations impossible to read.
issledovatelskaya-rukopis-content = [head=3]Tractatus de Revolutionibus: On the True Mechanics of the Celestial Spheres[/head]


    {"The dogma of our world's absolute immobility and central position in creation requires an absurd accumulation of epicycles, equants, and deferents. The wretchedness of the geocentric model becomes obvious to anyone capable of using fractions and trigonometry instead of blindly quoting church edicts. Empirical data obtained by means of precision dioptric apparatus mathematically proves the heliocentric nature of the system."}


    {"[bold]I. On the Kinematics of Wandering Lights and Optical Aberrations[/bold]"}

    {"Traditional doctrine is powerless to describe the retrograde motion of the outer planets, particularly the Crimson Wanderer. Taking our world as the center inevitably leads to the violation of fundamental laws of geometry. However, if the Daystar is placed at the focus of the orbital system, the anomaly is explained by a trivial difference in kinematic characteristics."}


    {"Let T be the sidereal period of our world's revolution, and P the orbital period of an outer planet. The observed synodic period S, the time between two astronomical oppositions, is calculated strictly:"}


    {"[color=#555555]█████▓▓▒▒░[/color]"}

    {"[color=#555555]█████████▓▓▒░░[/color]"}

staryy-dnevnik2-name = old diary
staryy-dnevnik2-desc = A small book with traces of soot on its pages. The author's signature at the very bottom has been carefully scraped away with a sharp blade, leaving a hole in the dense paper.
staryy-dnevnik2-content = [head=3]On the Mechanics of the Celestial Spheres and the Falsehood of the Central Dogma[/head]


    {"The dogmatists of the Church and the honorable magisters have comforted the people for centuries with tales that our world is an unmoving monolith, the navel of creation, around which the universe respectfully dances. They earnestly insist that the very stability of the Barrier rests upon our monumental stillness. Having devoted three decades to observations through a system of dioptric lenses, I have reached the only correct conclusion: it is astonishing how vast human vanity can grow when generously fertilized with ignorance."}


    {"One need only lift one's eyes from theological treatises and look into the eyepiece. The mechanics of the spheres do not know how to lie. If our world were the absolute center, the paths of wandering lights would present flawless arcs. In reality they regularly retreat, draw anomalous loops across the heavens, and cyclically change their brightness. Moreover, I have observed small moons circling distant planets with my own eyes. They dance in the icy void, entirely ignoring the pull of our world. Therefore, other centers of rotation exist within celestial mechanics."}


    {"We must admit the bitter truth for the proud: we do not sit upon the throne of Creation. Our world is merely a stone frigate, silently flying through the cosmic ocean around the true sovereign, the Daystar. We rotate. And the Barrier, despite the panicked shrieks of hierarchs, does not collapse from this motion, for it too obeys a single universal rhythm, not church edicts."}


    {"I harbor no illusions concerning my own fate. The Inquisition of Hellfire will gladly send me to the stake, and my instruments will be smashed to dust. So be it. The ash of my manuscripts and the heat of their fanatical pyres are too small a price for knowledge. They may burn an astronomer, but fortunately for us all, they cannot force the universe to stand still."}

